{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q137662114","formula":"C₂₁H₂₆BrNO₃","hill":"C21H26BrNO3","elements":["H","C","N","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":26.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"2C-B-3PIP-NBOMe"},"descriptions":{"en":"2C-B-3PIP-NBOMe is a serotonin receptor modulator of the phenethylamine, 2C, 3-phenylpiperidine (3PIP), and NBOMe families. It is a cyclized phenethylamine and along with 2C-B-3PIP-POMe is an NBOMe derivative of 2C-B-3PIP. The drug shows very weak affinity for the serotonin 5-HT2A and 5-HT2C receptors (Ki = 2,150 nM and 5,880 nM, respectively), with its affinities being profoundly reduced relative to those of 2C-B. The chemical synthesis of 2C-B-3PIP-NBOMe has been described. 2C-B-3PIP-NBOMe was first described in the scientific literature by Martin Hansen in 2010."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":"COc1cc(C2CCCN(Cc3ccccc3OC)C2)c(OC)cc1Br","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":null,"atoms":52,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":5.456,"y":3.107,"z":-1.431,"el":"C"},{"x":5.836,"y":1.746,"z":-1.577,"el":"O"},{"x":4.944,"y":0.787,"z":-1.177,"el":"C"},{"x":3.684,"y":1.051,"z":-0.632,"el":"C"},{"x":2.811,"y":0.009,"z":-0.242,"el":"C"},{"x":1.456,"y":0.403,"z":0.344,"el":"C"},{"x":1.312,"y":0.009,"z":1.822,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.056,"y":0.432,"z":2.35,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.188,"y":-0.083,"z":1.457,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.023,"y":0.383,"z":0.069,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.143,"y":-0.086,"z":-0.778,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.463,"y":0.6,"z":-0.469,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.517,"y":2.007,"z":-0.482,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.709,"y":2.68,"z":-0.224,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.865,"y":1.956,"z":0.042,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.831,"y":0.559,"z":0.05,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.638,"y":-0.129,"z":-0.207,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.521,"y":-1.495,"z":-0